title: With the setting on, a grammar from an extension colours a language the app knows too (here Rust, every word a number, what it leaves out in the plain colour); turned off under Highlighting, Rust is coloured by the app again
folders: grammars
extensions: grammar-extension
prefs: {"grammars_everywhere": true}
expect-log: the grammar of rust coloured src/main\.rs: 4 of its 4 lines tokenized
expect-log: the grammar of quill coloured src/hello\.quill
expect-log: script: colours of src/main\.rs line 2: number let · number answer · punct = · ident 42 · punct ; · comment // the answer$
expect-log: script: colours of src/hello\.quill line 3: keyword module · type Greeter$
expect-log: script: colours of src/main\.rs line 2: keyword let · ident answer · punct = · number 42 · punct ; · comment // the answer$
expect-file: {WORK}/data/prefs.json :: "grammars_everywhere": false

resize 1600 1000
wait 3000
colours src/hello.quill 1
goto src/main.rs
wait 2500
mark rust
wait 500
colours src/main.rs 2
colours src/hello.quill 3
left settings:highlighting
wait 1200
mark setting
wait 500
ui click 542 256
wait 500
mark setting-off
wait 500
left settings:close
wait 1000
colours src/main.rs 2
mark rust-own
wait 500
quit
